🔴 Vulnerability Title

Hardcoded LDAP Credentials in Configuration File

🔴 Description

It was observed that the application stores LDAP credentials, including username and password, in plaintext within the dataAddin.xml configuration file. These credentials are accessible via a shared network path used by the Excel add-in. The configuration exposes sensitive authentication details without encryption or protection. This indicates insecure credential handling and lack of secure configuration management.

🔴 Impact
Attackers can use exposed LDAP credentials to authenticate against directory services
Leads to unauthorized access to user information and internal resources
Increases risk of privilege escalation and further compromise
🔧 Mitigation
It is recommended to implement secure storage of LDAP credentials using a centralized secrets management solution instead of configuration files
Avoid hardcoding credentials and use secure authentication mechanisms such as Kerberos or integrated authentication
Restrict access to configuration files and ensure sensitive data is encrypted and properly protected
